---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import workspacePhoto from '../assets/photos/desk-speakers.jpg';
---

<Layout
  title="About"
  description="The Shed Studio is a San Diego-based music production studio, run by producer Hau Tran, built for sync licensing."
>
  <section class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl gap-12 px-6 pb-16 pt-20 md:grid-cols-[1fr_0.8fr] md:items-end md:px-10">
    <div>
      <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-brass-bright">About</p>
      <h1 class="mt-6 font-display text-4xl leading-tight text-paper md:text-5xl">
        One producer. Built to move fast.
      </h1>
    </div>
    <div class="relative aspect-[16/10] overflow-hidden rounded-sm">
      <Image
        src={workspacePhoto}
        alt="Hau at work in The Shed Studio, mixing at his desk"
        class="h-full w-full object-cover"
        widths={[400, 800, 1200]}
          quality={95}
        sizes="(min-width: 768px) 45vw, 100vw"
      />
      <div class="absolute inset-0 ring-1 ring-inset ring-paper/10"></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 pb-24 md:px-10">
    <div class="grid gap-16 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="space-y-6 text-ash">
        <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed">
          The Shed Studio is a San Diego-based music production studio run by
          producer Hau Tran. It started as a content and production practice
          — building an audience, learning what actually lands — and is now
          becoming what it was always headed toward: original music, made to
          order, for the people who need a track that fits a scene rather
          than one pulled from a stock library.
        </p>
        <p class="leading-relaxed">
          Every track is produced by hand. AI-assisted tools show up in the
          process — helping sketch ideas, explore a wider range of eras and
          genres faster than a solo producer working entirely unassisted —
          but the arrangement, the mix, and every final call are Hau's. It's
          a small studio, not a roster, and that's deliberate: one person
          who actually made the thing you're licensing, on the other end of
          every email.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="border border-paper/10 p-8">
        <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-brass-bright">Built for</p>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-paper">
          <li>Independent film & short films</li>
          <li>Game studios needing original score</li>
          <li>Animation & motion projects</li>
          <li>Trailers & campaign spots</li>
          <li>TV ads</li>
          <li>Paid ads</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-8 font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-brass-bright">Based in</p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-paper">San Diego, California</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
